{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And he called it Novach.</b> The 'לָה' has no matres lectionis heh, and I saw in the foundation of R. Moshe ha-Darshan: because this name was not established for it, therefore it is weak — for the implication of his midrash is like 'not.' And I wonder: what can be derived from two similar words — לָה 'וַיֹּאמֶר לָה בֹעַז' (Ruth 2), 'לִבְנוֹת לָה בַיִת' (Zechariah 5)?"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The 'matres lectionis heh' refers to the fact that לָה here is spelled ל-ה without a mappiq in the heh, indicating it lacks full orthographic status; Rashi's closing question challenges R. Moshe ha-Darshan's derivation by noting that the same weak spelling appears in ordinary contexts where no midrashic weakness is implied."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:37.410492263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}